1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,460
You've heard this one.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:05,464
A ghost ship is found with warm cups of tea still on the table.

3
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:06,520
Yeah.

4
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:07,971
That never happened.

5
00:00:09,371 --> 00:00:14,424
In eighteen eighty four, a young doctor wrote a short story about the Mary Celeste.

6
00:00:14,644 --> 00:00:20,157
He renamed her the Marie Celeste, invented passengers, and added a murderous villain.

7
00:00:20,657 --> 00:00:21,394
His name?

8
00:00:21,614 --> 00:00:22,875
Arthur Conan Doyle.

9
00:00:23,095 --> 00:00:24,513
The Sherlock Holmes guy.

10
00:00:25,013 --> 00:00:25,968
It was fiction.

11
00:00:26,188 --> 00:00:29,915
But people loved it so much, they mixed it up with the real thing.

12
00:00:31,315 --> 00:00:34,640
The men who actually boarded her found a wet, messy ship.

13
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:35,731
No meals.

14
00:00:35,951 --> 00:00:36,696
No tea.

15
00:00:36,916 --> 00:00:39,845
Just ten missing people and one lifeboat gone.

16
00:00:40,345 --> 00:00:43,766
Follow for the real stories behind history's legends.
